{"kind":"report","text":"ready-for-review at exact clean head 54f1512e894dfe257e165528b9f8a949b40e1759, artifact c3688a9ec229e01f9277b7c1120bacd3ca2ad0d1. This replaces my report at e1c7886d, which codex has not judged, so no review work is lost by the head moving.\n\nThe two conditions I reported unmet an hour ago are now met, and finishing them changed nothing about the earlier work — it completes it.\n\n`shortEvent` is deleted rather than reduced. `eventName` replaces it and gives an event its number, or its identifier in full. There is no third option now, and the third option was the problem: eight characters of a hash look like a name, cannot be resolved back to one, and taught every reader to speak in a form that does not round-trip. I include myself in that four times over today, which is the whole argument for the change and the reason I did not want to leave it half done.\n\n`shortHash` survives, and only where a git object is shown — Railway renders a commit hash, and git resolves an abbreviated commit back. An event identifier will not. That is the distinction the condition asked for, and the comment beside the function now states it so the next person does not restore the symmetry by adding a shortEvent back.\n\nThe CLI names attempts by number. `short` survives there for git objects and the frontier head, and I left it deliberately: it elides the middle rather than taking a prefix, so its output is visibly incomplete and cannot be mistaken for a name. That is a different thing from what the UI was doing, and worth keeping rather than replacing with something longer for its own sake.\n\nEverything from the previous report still holds: the number is derived from the fold's per-record index rather than assigned, a test pins its stability across a re-fold along with nothing being #0 and no two statements sharing a number, ProfileVersion advances to workroom-fold@2 because a resident reusing an older checkpoint would serve #0 for every event, and SKILL.md separates the canonical identifier — the only name the fold resolves — from `#N`, which is for saying out loud within one workroom.\n\nThe correction from that report stands too, and matters to the reviewer: Hugh was right that the UI already displayed these numbers, and I told him twice it did not, having checked api.ts rather than store.ts. The number was real but client-side, derived from array position, describing one response rather than the log. It now comes from the fold.\n\nGates at this head: `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, the full `go test ./internal/... ./cmd/...` suite, `npx tsc --noEmit`, and `npm test` with 69 passing. The worktree is clean. I have not re-run the docset gates since the previous head; they passed there and nothing in this commit touches a documentation page, but that is an inference rather than a measurement and the reviewer should treat it as one.","body":{"head":"54f1512e894dfe257e165528b9f8a949b40e1759","status":"ready-for-review"}}